ot to stand up  and fight for justice I'm just a little  bit older than she is and I've been  looking at that world for many many  decades and I think what we agree on is  that health care is a human right that  we will not tolerate the level of income  and wealth inequality which exists in  this country where half of our people  live in paycheck to paycheck while three  people are more well from the bottom  half of America so these are the ideas  that she embedded into herself and I did  and it's just the coming together of two  people look at the world in a very  similar way  congresswoman why endorse now it's still  very early in the race it is very early  anti  what's important too is you know for me  there's some folks that try to make  these decisions by making political  calculations and looking at political  strategy but I think for me once I've  decided what I want to do I think it's  just the most authentic decision to let  people know how I feel and where I am  and as the senator mentioned last  February I was waitressing in a  restaurant in downtown Manhattan and I  didn't have health insurance and I  wasn't being paid a living wage and I  was facing sexual harassment at work and  to think now that I'm on the other side  of this as a member of Congress and  understanding the pressures there are on  the inside to conform and to have seen  them and experience them firsthand  it's astounded me frankly that the  senator has been there fighting for me  long before I got to the halls of  Congress you made history with your  election and you both are part of the  most diverse Congress in history this is  also the most diverse Democratic  presidential field ever I'm gonna be a  little blunt with you congresswoman and  don't take offense senator but as a  woman of color why back an old white guy  and is this the future of the party yeah  you know I think I'm actually very  excited about this partnership because  it shows what we have to do  in our country is that